        "id": 1470474
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T20:31:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a little weird. If there\u0027s no surfacecontrols updated, then I think we still allocate a zero-length array of ASurfaceControl*s. It\u0027s not really NULL, but it\u0027s also not something a caller can dereference either.",
      "parentUuid": "c51def9d_01de440e",
      "revId": "010b135cb4ebd95ac5c4f3563d5ffdd0ceaba353",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c77a3661_ccc3c58c",
        "filename": "include/android/surface_control.h",
