      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 1496421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T21:39:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that makes the pointer to `ASurfaceControl*` nullable though, it\u0027ll just have a pointer to memory that should not be read per the length specified by `outASurfaceControlsSize`.\n\nRust has a similar concept IIRC.\n\nAfter all, what should we pass to the release function if it requires non-null `ASurfaceControl *` but this getter \"doesn\u0027t provide\" that?",
      "parentUuid": "a5b600aa_83b239bb",
      "revId": "010b135cb4ebd95ac5c4f3563d5ffdd0ceaba353",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
