      "writtenOn": "2024-05-19T18:53:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003e Shouldn\u0027t this be:\n\u003e\u003e ```\n\u003e\u003e ASurfaceControl* _Nullable* _Nullable* _Nonnull outASurfaceControls\n\u003e\u003e ```\n\u003e\n\u003e Isn\u0027t that what it is in the current patch set?\n\nDon\u0027t know how that got messed up, but the suggestion should have been:\n\n```\nASurfaceControl* _Nonnull* _Nullable* _Nonnull outASurfaceControls\n```\n\nSignifying that if there\u0027s an array of `ASurfaceControl*`s returned, those will all be nonnull pointers (with `*outASurfaceControlsSize` still stating how many one get back).\n\nAs Alec mentions however, it seems that the \"middle\" array pointer will (currently?) always be non-NULL, even though none of it should be dereferenced when `*outASurfaceControlsSize` is `0`.",
      "parentUuid": "e30bb8ad_cdd8315d",
      "revId": "010b135cb4ebd95ac5c4f3563d5ffdd0ceaba353",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4dadfae_6a084bda",
        "filename": "include/android/surface_control.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1496421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T10:07:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I started documenting semantics of NDK callbacks in https://github.com/rust-mobile/ndk/issues/464 and https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/318944941. I recall figuring out what these callbacks do, but haven\u0027t yet added the results to the table and will likely have to extract that again from my Rust wrapping and experiments with this API. Particularly:\n\n1. A user probably can\u0027t reset/remove the callback by setting `NULL` here?\n2. The callback will only be called _once_ (allowing us to clean up state directly at the end of the callback)?\n3. Will calling this function again _overwrite_ or _extend_ an existing callback?\n4. If the transaction is abandoned before being committed, the callback will not be called and the user should clean up any allocs/references in `context` themselves.\n\nSame question for the other callback.",
      "revId": "010b135cb4ebd95ac5c4f3563d5ffdd0ceaba353",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d63ff57_2b23d416",
        "filename": "include/android/surface_control.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1470474
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T20:31:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e A user probably can\u0027t reset/remove the callback by setting NULL here?\n\nNo, the callbacks are additive. They are removed when the framework invokes the callback.\n\n\u003e The callback will only be called once (allowing us to clean up state directly at the end of the callback)?\n\nCorrect they\u0027re only invoked once\n\n\u003e Will calling this function again overwrite or extend an existing callback?\n\nI suppose extend, although \"extend\" implies some ordering preservation which we don\u0027t guarantee.\n\n\u003e If the transaction is abandoned before being committed, the callback will not be called and the user should clean up any allocs/references in context themselves.\n\nIf by abandoned you mean that ASurfaceTransaction_apply() is not called prior to ASurfaceTransaction_delete(), then yes the transaction never made it downstream to the compositor so no callbacks are dispatched.",
      "parentUuid": "e4dadfae_6a084bda",
      "revId": "010b135cb4ebd95ac5c4f3563d5ffdd0ceaba353",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "237f5d7a_e984933d",
